# Problem log — mandatory for every agent

The repo root file `PROBLEM_LOG.md` is a **problem database** for future agent and human sessions.

**This rule applies to every agent that works in this repo** — parent Auto sessions, Cursor built-ins used on Nova work, and every Nova specialist (`daddy`, `tester`, `hod-momo`, `market-feed`, …). There is no exception by agent type or “quick fix” framing.

## Hard requirement

When a session **fixes or fully diagnoses** any of the following, the agent **MUST** prepend a new entry to `PROBLEM_LOG.md` in the **same session** as the fix (before or with the CHANGELOG / task-log / commit):

- Build, test, or linter failure
- Runtime or API error
- Incorrect behavior that required code or config changes
- A subtle root cause that would not be obvious on the next occurrence

**Skipping PROBLEM_LOG after a real fix is a constitution violation** — same severity as skipping CHANGELOG for a behavior change.

## Before deep debugging

**Search `PROBLEM_LOG.md` first** (repo search or open the file) for matching keywords or symptoms. If a prior entry fits, reuse that fix pattern when appropriate.

## Where and how

1. Prepend a new `##` section **immediately below** the `<!-- ENTRIES_START -->` marker (newest first).
2. Use the template in `PROBLEM_LOG.md`: Symptom, Cause, Fix, Keywords.
3. Do not log secrets, tokens, or personal data.
4. Cross-link from `CHANGELOG.md` / task-log `Related:` when those also get an entry.

## When skip is allowed

Only for:

- Purely cosmetic edits with **no** failure involved
- A one-line typo with **no** diagnostic story
- Status-only polls / read-only triage with **no** remediation

When skipping, Lifecycle (specialists) or the closing report (parent) **MUST** say `problem_log=skipped` or `problem_log=n/a` with a one-word reason when useful — never silently omit the declaration.

## Lifecycle declaration (specialists + parent reports that use Lifecycle)

Every Lifecycle footer **MUST** include:

```text
problem_log=<YYYY-MM-DD title or entry anchor>|skipped|n/a
```

Example after logging a fix:

```text
**Lifecycle:** memory=changed | promotion=none | dashboard=clean | handoff=none | task_log=knowledge/task-log/2026-07-23-example.md | problem_log=2026-07-23 — API_WEDGED
```

## Relationship to other logs

| Log | Answers |
|-----|---------|
| `PROBLEM_LOG.md` | What went wrong and how it was fixed (bugs / failures only) |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | What the codebase does now (every behavior change) |
| `knowledge/task-log/` | Full job narrative + why this approach |

A bug fix that changes behavior needs **PROBLEM_LOG + CHANGELOG** (and task-log when material). Do not treat CHANGELOG alone as satisfying this rule.

